{
  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "RFC 9530 Repr-Digest admission in requests and responses, including complete single/multipart ranges, before MCP dispatch/delivery; direct Go stream integrity and unavailable-representation denials. Local tests only, no deployment.",
  "standards": [
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9530.html#section-3",
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9530.html#section-3.1",
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html"
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Use the same bounded RFC 8941 byte-sequence dictionary parser for Content-Digest and Repr-Digest, with independent member sets and verification.",
    "Verify request representation bytes before signature inspection; require complete known coverage for a partial PUT. Direct Go egress snapshots the actual body before DNS for either integrity field.",
    "Verify ordinary response representation bytes; reconstruct a complete multipart representation only after proving bounded continuous coverage and consistent overlaps within that response.",
    "Deny Repr-Digest when full representation bytes are unavailable. HEAD/304 require explicit zero representation length and the empty hash; 204/205 with Repr-Digest are denied. Interim digest content uses empty representation data.",
    "Maintain sticky stream errors at EOF, preserve repeated Repr-Digest output values, and prevent Connection nomination of Repr-Digest. MIME fields stay separate.",
    "Keep JSON/XML, framing, range correlation, signatures and origin admission in force. No new Snort SID."
  ],
