  "limits": [
    "The RFC permits ignoring digests. Strong algorithms, duplicate-algorithm rejection and denial of unavailable representation data are stricter local policy; legitimate HTTP exchanges can be denied.",
    "Integrity fields remain optional and unsigned. A matching digest neither authenticates a sender nor establishes safe content; a hostile sender can omit or recompute it.",
    "No cross-response assembly, external resource retrieval, message signature verification, Want-* preference parsing or legacy Digest implementation is added.",
    "Streaming clients must discard bytes on any final read error. MCP buffers and validates before result delivery.",
    "Direct Go request cancellation relies on the caller Body contract that Close unblocks a concurrent Read. Digest-free direct transport behavior remains unchanged.",
    "Historical validation files preserve earlier source fingerprints. The final full-suite run covers the current sources; the focused Go run preceded only a generic diagnostic wording adjustment.",
    "No external endpoint, production routing boundary, universal W3C/RFC conformance or zero-day prevention was verified."
  ],
